      "position": 0,
      "content": "TRANSFER INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "df7b6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. Additional Resources: See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. Visit our Sac State Apply page for more information about our campus! Visit the Admissions website for current transfer admission requirements. Connect with an Admissions Counselor .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 32, 36); font-size: 14px;\">Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! </strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Additional Resources:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csus.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>University Catalog</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Sac State Apply</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> page for more information about our campus!</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit the </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/application-process/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions website</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for current transfer admission requirements. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Connect with an </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/connect-with-admissions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions Counselor</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. </span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "7f7a6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "MAJOR INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "817a6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The concentration in Ethics, Politics, and Law requires 18 units of elective courses. The majority of the elective courses are upper-division and must be taken at Sacramento State after transfer. PHIL 61 is the only lower-division elective that may be completed prior to transfer. The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Philosophy is compatible with the B.A. in Philosophy - Ethics, Politics, and Law concentration at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better. Students may complete PHIL 4 to meet CSU GE Area 1B (Critical Thinking). Students may complete PHIL 2, PHIL 6, or PHIL 26 to meet CSU GE Area 3B (Humanities). The minor in Philosophy requires 18 semester units. At least 9 units must be upper-division Philosophy courses. The lower-division Philosophy courses may overlap with general education requirements. Students may select up to 9 units of lower-division Philosophy courses from the following: PHIL 2, PHIL 4, PHIL 6, PHIL 26, PHIL 60, or PHIL 61. Please see an advisor for details. For additional information, please visit: Department of Philosophy .",
      "contentHtml": "<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">﻿The concentration in Ethics, Politics, and Law requires 18 units of elective courses. The majority of the elective courses are upper-division and must be taken at Sacramento State after transfer. PHIL 61 is the only lower-division elective that may be completed prior to transfer. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">﻿The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Philosophy is compatible with the B.A. in Philosophy - Ethics, Politics, and Law concentration at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students may complete PHIL 4 to meet CSU GE Area 1B (Critical Thinking). </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students may complete PHIL 2, PHIL 6, or PHIL 26 to meet CSU GE Area 3B (Humanities). </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The minor in Philosophy requires 18 semester units. At least 9 units must be upper-division Philosophy courses. The lower-division Philosophy courses may overlap with general education requirements. Students may select up to 9 units of lower-division Philosophy courses from the following: PHIL 2, PHIL 4, PHIL 6, PHIL 26, PHIL 60, or PHIL 61. Please see an advisor for details. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For additional information, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/arts-letters/philosophy/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Department of Philosophy</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></li></ol>"
    }
  ],
